  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/grblhal.cps` and `assets/posts/tormach.cps`: a G83 (deep peck) cycle with a positive dwell is refused by name. The refusal occurs before any G83 block is written.\n- The message text is the same as the Fanuc-family refusal in PR #2048: `canned cycle G83 (deep peck) dwell is not supported by this post - a <s> s dwell is refused, not dropped; set the dwell to 0`.\n- A G83 with no dwell posts as before. G82, G86 and G89 keep their P word in seconds.\n- `docs/decisions/2348-g83-dwell-linuxcnc.md` records the decision, the sources and the dropped alternatives.\n\n## Readings (public references only)\n\n- LinuxCNC G-code reference: `G83 (X- Y- Z-) or (U- V- W-) R- L- Q-`. There is no P word.\n- Tormach PathPilot G83 page: `G83 X~ Y~ Z~ A~ R~ L~ Q~`. There is no P word.\n- grblHAL core wiki and README: G83 is \"Drilling cycle with peck\". New codes follow the LinuxCNC specification. No P word is defined for G83.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/post/tests/g83_dwell_linuxcnc.rs` (2 tests, 2 passed):\n\n- `linuxcnc_family_refuses_a_g83_dwell_by_name`: tormach and grblhal, dwell 0.001 s and 0.5 s. The warning names G83 and the dwell. No G83 line is written. This test fails on the old post code (checked by a revert of the two post hunks).\n- `linuxcnc_family_posts_g83_without_dwell_unchanged`: dwell 0. One G83 block with Q, no P, no warnings.\n\n## Gate (local, debug, -j 6)\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post`: all binaries pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test conformance --test recorded_post_streams --test tormach_post --test grblhal_post --test post_cycle_feed_spindle`: all pass.\n- No golden `.nc` file changed. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real grblHAL or PathPilot control was run.\n- The full quick gate plan (821 steps, because the posts are embedded in all crates) was not run. Only the suites above were run.\n\n## Overlap\n\n- PR #2048 adds `crates/post/tests/g83_dwell.rs` and edits other posts. This PR does not touch those files. The test file has a different name, so the two PRs do not conflict.\n- PRs #2342 and #2346 also edit `assets/posts/tormach.cps`. The tormach hunk here is 5 added lines in `onCycle`, after the feed refusal.\n\nChangelog: The grblHAL and Tormach PathPilot posts now refuse a G83 (deep peck) dwell by name. Before, they dropped the dwell with no message.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2348\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
